# Build output.
#
# The binary patterns are anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored "eucd"
# matches every path element of that name, which silently excluded cmd/eucd/ — so the
# command's own source was never committed and every CI build failed on "cmd/eucd:
# directory not found".
/bin/
/dist/
/eucd
/eucd.exe

# Databases and exports are local working state, never committed. No workflow in this
# repository publishes a dataset: a public repository's logs, artifacts and release assets
# are all world-readable, so the crawl runs in a private one. See docs/running-a-crawl.md.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/export/

# Go
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Never. If one of these ever appears here, something is badly wrong.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.yaml
